; A type choice containing `bool` — pins the CLOSURE of the former "type annotations needed"
; (E0282) finding. `bool / tstr` and `uint / bool` once generated non-compiling Rust because the
; bool arm emitted `raw.bool().map_err(Into::into)`, whose intermediate error type is
; unconstrained where the expression's target type is inferred — and `DeserializeError` carries
; multiple `From<_>` impls, so inference fails (E0282/E0283). Fixed by emitting
; `bool::deserialize(raw)` instead (the `Primitive::Bool` arm in src/generation/deserialize.rs
; carries the load-bearing comment naming this class; bisect-verified against the pre-fix tree).
; Both bool-first (`bool / tstr`) and bool-last (`uint / bool`) orderings are exercised — the
; original finding named both spellings. Both now generate and round-trip under every profile
; (default / preserve / json). The canonical `type.choice` fixture stays `type_choice.cddl`
; (steered off `bool` to isolate the `/` construct itself, per the type_and_ranges.toml example
; note); this file isolates the bool-in-choice hazard specifically, so a regression re-introducing
; an unconstrained-error-type bool emission fails the corpus compile gate here rather than going
; unpinned.
bool_or_text = bool / tstr
uint_or_bool = uint / bool
